# HTTP Test Harness — Unified Service Scheduler
# Compatible with: VS Code REST Client, IntelliJ HTTP Client
# Install VS Code extension: "REST Client" by Huachao Mao
#
# Usage: Click "Send Request" above any ### block
# Seed data UUIDs from V2__seed_data.sql

@baseUrl = http://localhost:8080
@dealershipId_london = 11111111-0000-0000-0000-000000000001
@serviceType_oilChange = 22222222-0000-0000-0000-000000000001
@serviceType_brake = 22222222-0000-0000-0000-000000000002
@serviceType_overhaul = 22222222-0000-0000-0000-000000000003
@tech_alice = 33333333-0000-0000-0000-000000000001
@tech_bob = 33333333-0000-0000-0000-000000000002
@tech_carol = 33333333-0000-0000-0000-000000000003
@bay_a1 = 44444444-0000-0000-0000-000000000001
@bay_a2 = 44444444-0000-0000-0000-000000000002
@customer_james = 55555555-0000-0000-0000-000000000001
@customer_sarah = 55555555-0000-0000-0000-000000000002
@vehicle_civic = 66666666-0000-0000-0000-000000000001
@vehicle_corolla = 66666666-0000-0000-0000-000000000002

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# HEALTH & OBSERVABILITY
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

### [Health] Overall health check
GET {{baseUrl}}/q/health

### [Health] Liveness probe
GET {{baseUrl}}/q/health/live

### [Health] Readiness probe
GET {{baseUrl}}/q/health/ready

### [Metrics] Prometheus scrape endpoint
GET {{baseUrl}}/q/metrics

### [OpenAPI] Swagger UI (open in browser)
# http://localhost:8080/q/swagger-ui

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# FR-01: AVAILABILITY CHECK
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

### [FR-01] Check available slots — Oil Change (45min, skill 1)
# Expected: 200 OK with list of slots + Cache-Control: public, max-age=15
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/dealerships/{{dealershipId_london}}/availability?service_type_id={{serviceType_oilChange}}&start_date=2026-10-01&end_date=2026-10-07

### [FR-01] Check available slots — Brake Maintenance (60min, skill 3)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/dealerships/{{dealershipId_london}}/availability?service_type_id={{serviceType_brake}}&start_date=2026-10-01&end_date=2026-10-03

### [FR-01] Check available slots — Comprehensive Overhaul (120min, skill 7)
# Only Alice (skill 8) qualifies — Carol (2) and Bob (4) filtered out
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/dealerships/{{dealershipId_london}}/availability?service_type_id={{serviceType_overhaul}}&start_date=2026-10-01&end_date=2026-10-01

### [FR-01] ERROR: Missing required query params — should return 400
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/dealerships/{{dealershipId_london}}/availability

### [FR-01] ERROR: Invalid date range (end before start) — should return 400
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/dealerships/{{dealershipId_london}}/availability?service_type_id={{serviceType_oilChange}}&start_date=2026-10-07&end_date=2026-10-01

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# FR-02 + FR-03: BOOK APPOINTMENT WITH IDEMPOTENCY
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

### [FR-02] Happy Path: Book Oil Change — James Wilson, Alice, BAY-A1, Oct 1 09:00
# Expected: 201 Created with appointment details
# IMPORTANT: Generate a fresh UUID for Idempotency-Key on each new request
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/appointments
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: a1b2c3d4-e5f6-7890-abcd-ef1234567801

{
  "customerId":    "{{customer_james}}",
  "vehicleId":     "{{vehicle_civic}}",
  "dealershipId":  "{{dealershipId_london}}",
  "serviceTypeId": "{{serviceType_oilChange}}",
  "technicianId":  "{{tech_alice}}",
  "serviceBayId":  "{{bay_a1}}",
  "startTime":     "2026-10-01T09:00:00Z"
}

### [FR-03] IDEMPOTENCY: Same Idempotency-Key as above — must return SAME 201 response
# Even if sent 10 times, the result is identical (Redis cache hit, no DB write)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/appointments
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: a1b2c3d4-e5f6-7890-abcd-ef1234567801

{
  "customerId":    "{{customer_james}}",
  "vehicleId":     "{{vehicle_civic}}",
  "dealershipId":  "{{dealershipId_london}}",
  "serviceTypeId": "{{serviceType_oilChange}}",
  "technicianId":  "{{tech_alice}}",
  "serviceBayId":  "{{bay_a1}}",
  "startTime":     "2026-10-01T09:00:00Z"
}

### [FR-02] Book concurrent slot — Sarah Wilson, Bob, BAY-A2, SAME timeslot
# Expected: 201 Created (different tech+bay — no conflict)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/appointments
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: b2c3d4e5-f6a7-8901-bcde-f12345678902

{
  "customerId":    "{{customer_sarah}}",
  "vehicleId":     "{{vehicle_corolla}}",
  "dealershipId":  "{{dealershipId_london}}",
  "serviceTypeId": "{{serviceType_oilChange}}",
  "technicianId":  "{{tech_bob}}",
  "serviceBayId":  "{{bay_a2}}",
  "startTime":     "2026-10-01T09:00:00Z"
}

### [FR-02] CONFLICT: Same tech + same slot as first booking — should return 409
# Demonstrates: Two-tier defense working (Redis lock OR PG GiST exclusion catches this)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/appointments
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: c3d4e5f6-a7b8-9012-cdef-123456789003

{
  "customerId":    "{{customer_sarah}}",
  "vehicleId":     "{{vehicle_corolla}}",
  "dealershipId":  "{{dealershipId_london}}",
  "serviceTypeId": "{{serviceType_oilChange}}",
  "technicianId":  "{{tech_alice}}",
  "serviceBayId":  "{{bay_a2}}",
  "startTime":     "2026-10-01T09:00:00Z"
}

### [FR-02] ERROR: Missing Idempotency-Key header — should return 400
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/appointments
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "customerId":    "{{customer_james}}",
  "vehicleId":     "{{vehicle_civic}}",
  "dealershipId":  "{{dealershipId_london}}",
  "serviceTypeId": "{{serviceType_oilChange}}",
  "technicianId":  "{{tech_alice}}",
  "serviceBayId":  "{{bay_a1}}",
  "startTime":     "2026-10-01T09:00:00Z"
}

### [FR-02] ERROR: Invalid Idempotency-Key (not a UUID) — should return 400
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/appointments
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: not-a-valid-uuid

{
  "customerId":    "{{customer_james}}",
  "vehicleId":     "{{vehicle_civic}}",
  "dealershipId":  "{{dealershipId_london}}",
  "serviceTypeId": "{{serviceType_oilChange}}",
  "technicianId":  "{{tech_alice}}",
  "serviceBayId":  "{{bay_a1}}",
  "startTime":     "2026-10-01T09:00:00Z"
}

### [FR-02] ERROR: Past start time — should return 400 (Bean Validation: @Future)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/appointments
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: d4e5f6a7-b8c9-0123-defa-234567890004

{
  "customerId":    "{{customer_james}}",
  "vehicleId":     "{{vehicle_civic}}",
  "dealershipId":  "{{dealershipId_london}}",
  "serviceTypeId": "{{serviceType_oilChange}}",
  "technicianId":  "{{tech_alice}}",
  "serviceBayId":  "{{bay_a1}}",
  "startTime":     "2020-01-01T09:00:00Z"
}

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# FR-04: CANCEL APPOINTMENT
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# NOTE: Replace {appointmentId} with the UUID returned by the POST above

### [FR-04] Cancel appointment — update with actual ID from booking response
# Expected: 200 OK, status CANCELLED, slot restored in ES within 200ms
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/appointments/REPLACE-WITH-ACTUAL-APPOINTMENT-ID/status
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "status": "CANCELLED",
  "reason": "Customer requested cancellation via mobile application"
}

### [FR-04] ERROR: Appointment not found — should return 404
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/appointments/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000/status
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "status": "CANCELLED",
  "reason": "Test - non-existent appointment"
}

### [FR-04] ERROR: Invalid status value — should return 400
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/appointments/REPLACE-WITH-ACTUAL-APPOINTMENT-ID/status
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "status": "PENDING",
  "reason": "Invalid transition"
}

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# FULL SCENARIO: Book → Verify Conflict → Cancel → Verify Slot Restored
# Run these in sequence to test the complete booking lifecycle
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

### [SCENARIO Step 1] Book Alice for Oct 2 at 10:00
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/appointments
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: e5f6a7b8-c9d0-1234-efab-345678901005

{
  "customerId":    "{{customer_james}}",
  "vehicleId":     "{{vehicle_civic}}",
  "dealershipId":  "{{dealershipId_london}}",
  "serviceTypeId": "{{serviceType_oilChange}}",
  "technicianId":  "{{tech_alice}}",
  "serviceBayId":  "{{bay_a1}}",
  "startTime":     "2026-10-02T10:00:00Z"
}

### [SCENARIO Step 2] Try to book Alice for SAME slot → 409 Conflict
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/appointments
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: f6a7b8c9-d0e1-2345-fabc-456789012006

{
  "customerId":    "{{customer_sarah}}",
  "vehicleId":     "{{vehicle_corolla}}",
  "dealershipId":  "{{dealershipId_london}}",
  "serviceTypeId": "{{serviceType_oilChange}}",
  "technicianId":  "{{tech_alice}}",
  "serviceBayId":  "{{bay_a2}}",
  "startTime":     "2026-10-02T10:00:00Z"
}

### [SCENARIO Step 3] Cancel Alice's booking (use ID from Step 1 response)
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/appointments/REPLACE-WITH-STEP1-ID/status
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "status": "CANCELLED",
  "reason": "Testing slot release"
}

### [SCENARIO Step 4] Now book Alice for the SAME slot again → 201 (slot released)
# Wait ~200ms for ES sync before checking availability
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/appointments
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: a7b8c9d0-e1f2-3456-abcd-567890123007

{
  "customerId":    "{{customer_sarah}}",
  "vehicleId":     "{{vehicle_corolla}}",
  "dealershipId":  "{{dealershipId_london}}",
  "serviceTypeId": "{{serviceType_oilChange}}",
  "technicianId":  "{{tech_alice}}",
  "serviceBayId":  "{{bay_a1}}",
  "startTime":     "2026-10-02T10:00:00Z"
}
